  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 145 PM Monday... \n\nKEY MESSAGE 1... A Frost Advisory is in effect from 1 AM to 8 AM \nTuesday across much of central NC, with the exception of our far SE.\n\nCool surface high pressure will remain over the Southeast US through \ntonight, with any cloud cover associated with a shortwave \ndisturbance remaining well to our north over the Northeast US. Given \nW/NW winds turning mainly calm and a stout surface inversion \ndeveloping after dark, the stage should be set for ideal radiational \ncooling conditions tonight. Low temperatures this morning were in \nthe mid-30s in some outlying areas (including 33F at Burlington and \nSiler City), and while low-level thicknesses will be about 5-10 m \nhigher tonight, winds should be calmer given the surface high nosing \nfarther NE into the region. So expect lows in the mid-to-upper-30s \nacross most of central NC outside of urban areas and the far SE \nwhere they should be closer to 40. Thus issued a Frost Advisory from \n1 AM to 8 AM Tuesday for all our counties except the far SE from \nScotland east to Sampson counties.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2... Cold front will bring low-end rain chances on \nThursday, followed by the coldest air so far this season for the \nweekend.\n\nA cold front will sweep across central NC during the daytime \nThursday.  Given the antecedent dry air and modest pwat and limited \nprefrontal moisture advection, PoPs assoc with the fropa will remain \nsub-50%. For areas that do receive some rainfall, amounts will be \nless than 1/2 inch. \n\nVigorous CAA is expected behind the cold front, with H8 temps \nfalling from around +10C pre-frontal to around -4C post-frontal by \nFriday night. This will be the coldest airmass so far this season. \nWith high pressure building over the Carolinas by Sunday, low temps \nSunday morning will be the coldest in this string of cold days, with \nat- or sub-freezing low temps expected Sunday morning which will end \nthe growing season across central NC.  To summarize post-frontal \ntemps... look for highs in the 50s Friday through Monday, with low \ntemps in the lower 30s Saturday morning, Sunday morning and Monday \nmorning.",
